From d0aa8b6a4b5247455e43653895e27473525620f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:06:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1016/1178] Form trimming: idea writer retired, one slider per
 adapter half, TAB skips the tips
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HERESY 1016.
- "Start from an idea" leaves the Create form (its code stays, dormant). Its
  section templates live on in the writing room: a Structure choice whose
  per-section rules (four-line chorus, identical each time; instrumental
  intro and outro as a bare tag…) are added to the brief.
- An adapter shows only the slider of the half its file has: a sound-only
  LoRA no longer carries a dead music slider, and the column stops swelling.
- Guidance (CFG) loses its long hint ("1.0 for full and melody…"), which the
  tip already says and which stretched the field and broke Reset sampling.
- The (i) marks leave the tab order: TAB goes from field to field and no tip
  pops up on the way. Hovering still shows them.
- The spectrum's pictures stay hidden until there is something on them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
